{
  "_readme": [
    "Kit prose: every word the Kits can return, enumerated by sweeping each classifier across its",
    "whole domain (not by reading the source), so no band can be missing.",
    "",
    "Scale codes stay verbatim inside the string — 'G1 Minor' becomes 'G1 Gering', never 'S1 Gering'.",
    "Where a language inflects the adjective, R and S carry the gender of that language's own noun:",
    "R is a radio blackout (uk радіозатемнення n., pl zaciemnienie n., cs výpadek m., es apagón m.,",
    "it blackout m., pt apagão m., fr coupure f.) while G and S are storms (mostly feminine).",
    "That is why the R block is not a copy of the G block with the letter swapped."
  ],
